From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ARM: dts: gts28ltexx: the GPU on the G3D PLL, 160 to 700
 MHz

With mout_g3d_pll parked on OSCCLK whenever the G3D PLL is off or
relocking, the GPU can run from the PLL again, at the vendor kernel's
eight Mali levels instead of the 100-400 MHz that aclk_g3d_400 divides
to.  At panfrost's probe the GPU mux moves onto mout_g3d_pll, the PLL
goes to 160 MHz while it is off and the GPU divider to 1; aclk_g3d_400,
CMU_G3D's register clock, stays at 400 MHz.

Voltages: this chip's stock G3D values (ASV table version 8, group 1)
plus 37.5 mV, what stock itself programs on this chip when cold:
160 MHz 912.5 mV, 266 925, 350 950, 420 975, 500 1000, 550 1025,
600 1075 and 700 MHz 1175 mV, under BUCK6's 1.2 V stock ceiling.  The
G3D sensor is disabled, so stock's KFC rule on the A53 sensor (81 C:
420 MHz at most, 86 C: 160 MHz) and the A57 sensors' 95 and 100 C trips
(the same caps) stand in for stock's G3D caps.

glmark2 on the SM-T715 (2026-11-07), each level pinned: 125 at 160 MHz,
328 at 266, 424 at 350, 501 at 420, 586 at 500, 637 at 550, 686 at 600
and 781 at 700 MHz, at 63 C at most; no fault but Mesa's known
DATA_INVALID job faults, seen at every clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi    | 162 ++++++++++++------
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig         |   2 +-
 2 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
index a3ad3f9ac..3871c6774 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
  *
  * Enables the SoC's gpu@14ac0000 node (exynos5433.dtsi:1186-1235) for the
  * mainline panfrost driver, with frequency and voltage scaling on the G3D
- * bus clock (100 to 400 MHz, below) and BUCK6 as its rail.  docs/GPU.md
+ * PLL (160 to 700 MHz, below) and BUCK6 as its rail.  docs/GPU.md
  * has the source tables and the reasoning.
  *
  * Stock reference (01_dumps/live_fdt.dts:1830-1836, node "mali"): same
@@ -32,98 +32,152 @@ &gpu {
 	 * and the regulator the stock Mali platform code drives
 	 * (kernel_universal5433 drivers/gpu/arm/t7xx/r22p0/platform/exynos/
 	 * gpu_exynos5433.c:683, regulator_get(NULL, "vdd_g3d")).  The board
-	 * file keeps it always-on at the bootloader voltage (600-1500 mV
-	 * window, no voltage request from anyone).  With no OPP table below,
-	 * panfrost only takes an enable reference on it
-	 * (panfrost_device.c:86-117, 225-230) and never sets a voltage.
-	 * The phandle also orders the GPU probe after the PMIC.
+	 * file keeps it always on (600-1500 mV window); the OPP table below
+	 * sets its voltage at each level.  The phandle also orders the GPU
+	 * probe after the PMIC.
 	 */
 	mali-supply = <&buck6_reg>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	/*
-	 * The G3D block runs from CMU_TOP's aclk_g3d_400, not from the G3D
-	 * PLL the bootloader left at 266 MHz.  CMU_G3D's own registers are
-	 * clocked from that same mux: with the PLL behind it, gating the GPU
-	 * clock stopped the PLL (pll_35xx has a disable op) and CMU_G3D's
-	 * runtime suspend, which reads its registers next, hung the bus at
-	 * panfrost's first runtime suspend (2026-11-04).  From aclk_g3d_400,
-	 * which CMU_G3D holds while it is resumed (clk-exynos-arm64.c
-	 * exynos_arm64_cmu_resume()), the registers keep a clock until the
-	 * unit has switched itself to OSCCLK and released it.  The mux never
-	 * moves back to the PLL on a rate request (CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT in
-	 * clk-exynos5433.c).
+	 * The GPU runs from the G3D PLL (mout_aclk_g3d_400 on mout_g3d_pll),
+	 * at the vendor kernel's eight Mali levels, 160 to 700 MHz.  The PLL
+	 * path hung the bus once (2026-11-04): gating the GPU clock stopped
+	 * the PLL while the mux still selected it, and CMU_G3D's own
+	 * registers are clocked from that tree.  mout_g3d_pll now moves to
+	 * OSCCLK by itself whenever the PLL is off or relocking
+	 * (clk-exynos5433.c, exynos5433_g3d_register_park()), as the vendor
+	 * kernel did by hand.
 	 *
-	 * aclk_g3d_400 is the bus PLL (800 MHz) divided by 2, its nominal
-	 * 400 MHz, and the GPU clock divides it again in CMU_G3D (DIV_G3D,
-	 * 1 to 8): 400, 200, 133 and 100 MHz, the OPPs below.  The GPU
-	 * divider is set first, so the GPU never runs at 400 MHz on the
-	 * bootloader's voltage: 266/2 = 133 MHz, then 400/2 = 200 MHz, where
-	 * devfreq starts (panfrost_devfreq.c, the current rate).
+	 * At panfrost's probe, of_clk_set_defaults() sets the parents, then
+	 * the rates in this order: the GPU mux onto mout_g3d_pll, which sits
+	 * on OSCCLK while nothing is enabled; the PLL to 160 MHz while it is
+	 * off; the GPU divider to 1, so 160 MHz; aclk_g3d_400, CMU_TOP's bus
+	 * clock into the block and CMU_G3D's register clock, at its nominal
+	 * 400 MHz.  devfreq starts at 160 MHz, the lowest OPP, which any
+	 * voltage the rail may hold then (912.5 mV or more) carries.
 	 */
 	assigned-clocks = <&cmu_g3d CLK_MOUT_ACLK_G3D_400>,
+			  <&cmu_g3d CLK_FOUT_G3D_PLL>,
 			  <&cmu_g3d CLK_DIV_ACLK_G3D>,
 			  <&cmu_top CLK_DIV_ACLK_G3D_400>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&cmu_top CLK_ACLK_G3D_400>, <0>, <0>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <0>, <133333333>, <400000000>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&cmu_g3d CLK_MOUT_G3D_PLL>, <0>, <0>, <0>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <0>, <160000000>, <160000000>, <400000000>;
 
 	/* the NoC timeout that a power-off of pd_g3d clears (panfrost_gpu.c) */
 	samsung,sysreg = <&sysreg_g3d>;
 
 	/*
-	 * GPU frequency scaling on the bus clock (simple_ondemand).  The SoC
-	 * table is the stock Mali driver's default, on the G3D PLL; this board
-	 * replaces it.  Voltages: this chip's stock G3D values (ASV table
-	 * version 8, group 1, printed by stock at every boot; docs/hardware/
-	 * GPU.md section 10.3) plus 37.5 mV, stock's own cold margin, each OPP
-	 * on the stock level at or above it: 400 MHz on 420 MHz's 937.5 mV
-	 * (+37.5 = 975 mV), 200 MHz on 266 MHz's 887.5 mV (925 mV), 133 and
-	 * 100 MHz on 160 MHz's 875 mV (912.5 mV).  400 MHz is below stock's
-	 * first thermal cap (420 MHz from 95 C on the G3D sensor).
+	 * GPU frequency scaling (simple_ondemand) on the vendor kernel's
+	 * levels, with the vendor's P, M and S for the G3D PLL.  Voltages:
+	 * this chip's own stock G3D values (ASV table version 8, group 1,
+	 * printed by stock at every boot; docs/hardware/GPU.md section 10.3)
+	 * plus 37.5 mV, stock's cold margin: what stock itself programs on
+	 * this chip at or below 19 C.  The 100-400 MHz bus-clock table of
+	 * kernel #7 ran these voltages at 133-400 MHz on 2026-11-07.  Stock
+	 * kept 700 MHz for its counter-driven boost and capped the rest at
+	 * 600 MHz; simple_ondemand uses 700 MHz whenever the GPU is busy.
 	 */
-	operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table_bus>;
+	operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table_pll>;
 	#cooling-cells = <2>;
 	/delete-node/ opp-table;
 
-	gpu_opp_table_bus: opp-table-gpu-bus {
+	gpu_opp_table_pll: opp-table-gpu-pll {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
-		opp-100000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <100000000>;
+		opp-160000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <160000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <912500>;
 		};
 
-		opp-133333333 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <133333333>;
-			opp-microvolt = <912500>;
+		opp-266000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <266000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <925000>;
 		};
 
-		opp-200000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <200000000>;
-			opp-microvolt = <925000>;
+		opp-350000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <350000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <950000>;
 		};
 
-		opp-400000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <400000000>;
+		opp-420000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <420000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <975000>;
 		};
+
+		opp-500000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <500000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1000000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-550000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <550000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1025000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1075000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-700000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <700000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1175000>;
+		};
 	};
 };
 
 /*
- * GPU cooling, stock's KFC rule (exynos_thermal.c:997-1000): from 86 C on
- * the A53 sensor, the GPU at its slowest level, beside the A53s' own map
- * on the same trip (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi, included before
- * this file).  devfreq cooling counts from the fastest OPP: 0 = 400,
- * 1 = 200, 2 = 133, 3 = 100 MHz.  The G3D sensor is disabled
- * (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-thermal.dtsi), and stock's 95-110 C G3D caps
- * start at 420 MHz, above this table.
+ * GPU cooling.  The G3D sensor is disabled
+ * (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-thermal.dtsi), so stock's G3D caps (420 MHz from
+ * 95 C, down to 160 MHz from 110 C) have no sensor here; what stands in:
+ *  - stock's KFC rule (exynos_thermal.c:991-1000): from 81 C on the A53
+ *    sensor, the GPU at 420 MHz at most, from 86 C at 160 MHz, on the
+ *    trips of the A53s' own maps (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi,
+ *    included before this file);
+ *  - the A57 sensors' 95 and 100 C trips, the same two caps: not stock,
+ *    a guard for a GPU that heats the die with no sensor of its own.
+ * devfreq cooling counts from the fastest OPP: 0 = 700, 1 = 600, 2 = 550,
+ * 3 = 500, 4 = 420, 5 = 350, 6 = 266, 7 = 160 MHz.
  */
 &apollo_thermal {
 	cooling-maps {
+		map-gpu-420 {
+			trip = <&apollo_a53_1g>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 4 4>;
+		};
+
 		map-gpu-min {
 			trip = <&apollo_a53_min>;
-			cooling-device = <&gpu 3 3>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 7 7>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&atlas0_thermal {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-gpu-420 {
+			trip = <&atlas0_a53_1g>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 4 4>;
+		};
+
+		map-gpu-min {
+			trip = <&atlas0_a53_min>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 7 7>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&atlas1_thermal {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-gpu-420 {
+			trip = <&atlas1_a53_1g>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 4 4>;
+		};
+
+		map-gpu-min {
+			trip = <&atlas1_a53_min>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 7 7>;
 		};
 	};
 };
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index f1a5783d4..b30ce4e59 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -184,7 +184,7 @@ CONFIG_RMI4_F12=y
 CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST=m
 
 # GPU frequency scaling: panfrost devfreq over the board's OPP table, on
-# the G3D bus clock (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi, 100 to 400 MHz).
+# the G3D PLL (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi, 160 to 700 MHz).
 # PM_DEVFREQ is also selected by panfrost and selects PM_OPP.  panfrost's
 # governor built in, so devfreq_add_device() needs no request_module() at
 # panfrost load (drivers/devfreq/devfreq.c); the devfreq cooling device,
-- 
